    "result": {
      "ok": true,
      "stdout": "Detect music beats or melody points.\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n          --ref TEXT          Unified draft reference\r\n          --seg-id TEXT       Target segment id (required; raw id, no seg_id= prefix)\r\n          --level TEXT        Algorithm level, e.g. 0 / 1 / 2\r\n          --mode TEXT         Detection target: beat (rhythm points) / melody (melody points)\r\n          --level-count TEXT  Beat level granularity: 2 or 5 (default 5). When 2, --level must\r\n                              be 0 or 1\r\n          --apply TEXT        Apply detected beat points to the draft: true / false\r\n          --return-beats-info TEXT \r\n                              Return detected beat details: true / false\r\n          --need-audio-has-music TEXT \r\n                              Require music-content detection: true / false\r\n          --music-id TEXT     Music material id\r\n          --music-beat-query TEXT \r\n                              Music beat query mode\r\n          --upload-vid TEXT   Uploaded media vid\r\n          --output-dir TEXT   Directory for beat-analysis output\r\n          --timeout <duration> \r\n                              Beat-analysis timeout; explicit unit required (us, ms, s, min)\r\n          --poll-interval <duration> \r\n                              Beat-analysis poll interval; explicit unit required (us, ms, s,\r\n                              min)\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  # Detect beat points at detection level 2\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft algo music-beats --mode beat --level 2 --seg-id <UUID>\r\n  # Detect melody points\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft algo music-beats --mode melody --seg-id <UUID>\r\n  # Use the coarse 2-level granularity (level must be 0 or 1)\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft algo music-beats --mode beat --level-count 2 --level 1 --seg-id <UUID>\r\n  # Return beat details without applying them\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft algo music-beats --mode beat --apply false --return-beats-info true --seg-id <UUID>\r\n",
      "stderr": "",
      "output": "Detect music beats or melody points.\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n          --ref TEXT          Unified draft reference\r\n          --seg-id TEXT       Target segment id (required; raw id, no seg_id= prefix)\r\n          --level TEXT        Algorithm level, e.g. 0 / 1 / 2\r\n          --mode TEXT         Detection target: beat (rhythm points) / melody (melody points)\r\n          --level-count TEXT  Beat level granularity: 2 or 5 (default 5). When 2, --level must\r\n                              be 0 or 1\r\n          --apply TEXT        Apply detected beat points to the draft: true / false\r\n          --return-beats-info TEXT \r\n                              Return detected beat details: true / false\r\n          --need-audio-has-music TEXT \r\n                              Require music-content detection: true / false\r\n          --music-id TEXT     Music material id\r\n          --music-beat-query TEXT \r\n                              Music beat query mode\r\n          --upload-vid TEXT   Uploaded media vid\r\n          --output-dir TEXT   Directory for beat-analysis output\r\n          --timeout <duration> \r\n                              Beat-analysis timeout; explicit unit required (us, ms, s, min)\r\n          --poll-interval <duration> \r\n                              Beat-analysis poll interval; explicit unit required (us, ms, s,\r\n                              min)\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\